{"agent":"lane-drift-a","data":{"by":"lane-drift-a","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":2,"detail":"The new landed-change guard only fails closed when `HEAD` is exactly the base branch head. If the item has already been merged but is being evaluated from a worktree whose `HEAD` is still the merged item commit (an ancestor of `base`), the equality test is false and the guard does not fire. Example: item branch commit `A` adds logic; after landing, `base` is `A` plus a docs-only commit `D` outside the item's logic paths. Calling this function from the item worktree with `item.base = base` sees `head.out != basecommit.out`, continues to `_is_format_or_comment(tree, base, paths)`, and that comparison over the item's paths sees no AST change, so it can return True. The already-landed logic change is then still classified trivial, defeating the stated fix. The check should fail closed when the item's committed change is already contained in `base` (e.g. ancestor/empty `base...HEAD`), not only when the two SHAs are equal.","digest":"c97947676f0a8f92","location":"ddflow/services/docsonly.py:89","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/docsonly.py:89"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"The new holder-consent bypass trusts the caller-supplied `queued_by` string without proving that the call is the queue integrator or that a matching queue entry exists. Given an item with a live lease held by agent `A`, another agent `B` can call `merge(..., agent=\"B\", queued_by=\"A\")`; `LS.peer_live_lease` returns `A`'s lease, `_queued_by_holder` returns true, and the lease-refusal branch is skipped, letting `B` land `A`'s branch and end `A`'s lease.","digest":"5d01fe3380f732c5","location":"ddflow/api/lifecycle/merge.py:250","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/api/lifecycle/merge.py:250"}],"chunks_total":7,"coverage":"6/7 chunk(s) reviewed","diff_sha":"7b4b170939847f19400848d356cdcdb9c468ce19bbf953b3577b41bccf0c1b05","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"max_chunk_c